{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9746-how-a-demon-dies","id":9746,"title":"How a Demon Dies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-13T09:07:35-08:00","id":9746,"title":"How a Demon Dies","content":"Hey all, I'm not sure if it's mentioned in the PDF but I can't seem to find the part that tells you how Demons heal, and what happens when they die? Unless I'm not reading this pre-book-PDF properly?<br /> <br /> Totally happy that we've been given it, btw! I'm engrossed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/933-shadowhowler","name":"shadowhowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar933_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T09:11:33-08:00","id":9748,"title":"","content":"Outside of demonic form, Unchained heal like dudes.<br /> <br /> I don't recall what happens to their Covers when they die, but the demon itself just dies, as far as I remember. They don't leave ghosts or nothin'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","name":"Metrophelean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:05:46-08:00","id":9792,"title":"","content":"I found this:<br /> <br /> &quot;The demon heals lethal or bashing damage equal to her Primum rating, starting with the rightmost health box upon changing into her demonic form. Any Tilts relating to a bodily injury, such as Arm Wrack, are removed.&quot;<br /> <br /> So that explains some natural healing. I guess Death is just death since it says that any wounds suffered go with you from Cover to Cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/933-shadowhowler","name":"shadowhowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar933_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T12:40:03-08:00","id":9915,"title":"","content":"For that healing: It is only when you assume full demonic form (partial is not enough). I cleared that earlier today.<br /> <br /> Also if they die while in cover or in demonic form they are dead just normal dead. Although good question what happens with all covers AND also what happens when they die in demonic form (do they change then automatically into their last cover? [if so what is up when they have burnt their last cover by going loud?])","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T14:38:44-08:00","id":9990,"title":"","content":"Dying outside of Cover makes more work for the God-Machine's agents who have to clean up these kind of messes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T15:01:26-08:00","id":10005,"title":"","content":"A Demon in cover heals like a human, barring the use of Embeds or Exploits. Taking demonic form immediately heals [Primum] lethal or bashing damage, but doesn't increase healing speed unless they have a form power that does so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T16:26:23-08:00","id":10066,"title":"","content":"I couldve sworn in the development phase, one of the devs said that a demon who dies loses that cover but still goes on, and is okay if he can get a new one. is that gone, or does it apply only to covers dying of old age?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T17:15:02-08:00","id":10087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9746-how-a-demon-dies?p=10066#post10066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I couldve sworn in the development phase, one of the devs said that a demon who dies loses that cover but still goes on, and is okay if he can get a new one. is that gone, or does it apply only to covers dying of old age?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the draft's page 23: <i>&quot;Demons age along with their human Cover and die of old age if their Cover does. Theoretically, demons can achieve great longevity by changing to a youthful Cover every few decades, but even the eldest Unchained can still die to accident or violence.&quot;</i> A later section on switching identities clarifies that it won't heal any actual damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">(Previously known by the name of &quot;GrimGent&quot;.)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/335-the-yann-waters","name":"The Yann Waters","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T17:38:46-08:00","id":10099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Yann Waters</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9746-how-a-demon-dies?p=10087#post10087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the draft's page 23: <i>&quot;Demons age along with their human Cover and die of old age if their Cover does. Theoretically, demons can achieve great longevity by changing to a youthful Cover every few decades, but even the eldest Unchained can still die to accident or violence.&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div><i><b>BRING ME THE SOUL OF A FORSAKEN CHILD</b></i><br /> <br /> Edit: Know what could be neat to see? A demon who painstakingly splices together pacts over time to keep recreating more-or-less-the-same Covers as their current one ages too much to be useful. You could play this up as slightly deranged or explain it as sign of how the Demon really identifies with that Cover and is really uncomfortable with the short, transient lifespans of mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":478,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","user":"Intrepid Vector","date":". 11-13-2013, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/478-intrepid-vector","name":"Intrepid Vector","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar478_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T18:27:10-08:00","id":10964,"title":"","content":"I have yet to read far enough into the book to reach the stuff about the actual Demon template and its features, however to make sure I have this correct -<br /> <br /> In Cover a Demon heals exactly like a normal mortal. I take it they are also subject to the knock-out/bleeding out rules for getting a health track full of bashing/lethal? <br /> <br /> In Demonic Form they heal a number of Bashing/Lethal damage equal to their Primum when they transform and loose any tilts resulting from injury. <br /> <br /> If they die in Demonic Form they are perma dead.<br /> <br /> If they die in cover they are perma dead (and don't just pop into the next cover or Demonic Form?)<br /> <br /> When in Demonic Form they still heal at the same rate as a human being for the different types of damage?<br /> <br /> How many Embeds/Exploits/Demonic Form Powers are there that let you heal?<br /> <br /> Just that at the moment they are sounding pretty flimsy. <br /> <br /> As you can switch back and forth to Demon form, but that is going to shred your cover and unless you have high Primum does not seem to be either worth it or a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T18:40:05-08:00","id":10970,"title":"","content":"On the Mend is pretty powerful. It lets you heal all bashing with a success, one lethal per success or agg equal to your primum. an exceptional success is recover all bashing plus a will power, recover all health lost to lethal or point of agg damage per succes or primum whichever is higher. Thats just an embed.<br /> <br /> Just Bruised on a single success on any damage you take or a target takes to just one. <br /> <br /> Shift Consequences can redirect damage as well and that's an embed<br /> <br /> Break to Heal also is pretty powerful as a healing tool but that's an exploit.<br /> <br /> Demons aren't to squishy IMO.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":991,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","user":"pgolasze13","date":". 11-14-2013, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T18:44:27-08:00","id":10972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9746-how-a-demon-dies?p=10964#post10964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have yet to read far enough into the book to reach the stuff about the actual Demon template and its features</div> </div> </div> </div>Stopping you here because in my experience this is where people start putting their feet in their mouths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just that at the moment they are sounding pretty flimsy. </div> </div> </div>Demonic form powers can include things like armor, regeneration, teleportation, Defense boosts \u2014 and they can be customized to include these things every time their Primum goes up or down. Most of those aren't even mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> Break to Heal and Halo are both healing or recovery-accelerating Exploits, and On the Mend is an Embed \u2014 which suffer no untrained Skill penalties and don't cost Aether \u2014 that can at the very least heal a point of lethal or aggravated damage or <i>all</i> of your bashing damage.<br /> <br /> If a demon lives the sort of life where they expect to face injury on a regular basis, it's not hard for them to prepare against that eventuality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-14-2013, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T18:48:29-08:00","id":10975,"title":"","content":"Between On the Mend, Just a bruise, Break to Heal, and Tough as stone it feels to me like demons can recover from injuries very quickly.<br /> <br /> That's not even considering abilities like Never Here, 4 Minutes ago, and Echoing Death which allow them to completely reset damage taken and resources...<br /> <br /> Oh..and if you Go Loud all injuries are healed...along with boosting your Primium to the the max and refilling aether...of course losing a cover is never desirable, but the option is there!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1092,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1092-tribute-of-a-dark-heart","user":"Tribute of a Dark Heart","date":". 11-14-2013, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1092-tribute-of-a-dark-heart","name":"Tribute of a Dark Heart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1092_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T18:52:15-08:00","id":10978,"title":"","content":"All of this is true. It still feels to me like demons are the major supernatural line of the nWoD to most worry about the consequences of any fight they get themselves into - the stakes feel higher, no fight feels trivial. Perhaps this opinion will change when I actually start running the game and see the healing powers in action, but I like that notion. It adds some of the tension back in that can be lost, without being so lethal that the chronicle is ended prematurely or the characters have to spend frequent weeks of downtime healing up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T18:59:37-08:00","id":10980,"title":"","content":"Well it's a game of techgnostic espionage so it's very fitting. I feel that mages and demons are similar in that catch one unprepared it could be a cake walk, but if they had the opportunity to prepare? God rest the poor bastards soul that pissed either of them off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T19:47:11-08:00","id":11004,"title":"","content":"So if I have this right...<br /> <br /> So we have the following Embeds that either heal or negate damage in some way - On the Mend, Just Bruised, Shift Consiquences (Cover Check +1), Never Here (Only in certain circumstances), <br /> <br /> The following Exploits that do the same - Break to Heal, Halo (Long Term Healing), 4 Minutes Ago, Echoing Death<br /> <br /> The following Demonic Traits that do the same - Tough as Stone, Armour Plates, Huge Size (adds +4 Health), Slippery Body (Only Grapples), Electric Jolt (specialist Armour), The Resistances (Complete Immunity from certain sources of damage), Phasing, Plasma Drive, Teleportation (if used smartly), Aegis Protocol, Extra Mechanical Limbs, Wound Healing. <br /> <br /> Going Loud and its unique stuff. <br /> <br /> So yeah, quite a few ways of dealing with damage. Though of course, the majority of these are Demonic Form abilities which means Compromise rolls. Still, having four powers that you can use without Compromise rolls (most of the time) is pretty decent. <br /> <br /> I do have a question about the Wound Healing Demonic Form Trait. It says you can heal wounds reflexively then mentions that you heal the right most box filled with bashing or lethal. Is this the reflexive healing? Or is it an addition affect and you can spend Aether to heal damage or use other healing abilities as a reflexive action that turn? As healing one bashing or lethal a turn is alright, but compared with some of the other demonic form abilities is not that great. <br /> <br /> I agree with Stupid Loserman that despite having about 20+ different ways of either ignoring, downgrading, reversing or healing damage Demons do still feel like they have more to loose in a fight. My main WoD game for the last year has been Mummy, which is perhaps the toughest core template, so I guess I have been a bit desensitized to damage related stuff. Even Vampires seem pretty tough with the new rules update (if previews are anything to go by) and I suspect Werewolves will only get tougher with their update.<br /> <br /> I'd say Demon's are on the same level as Changeling or Mage for &quot;toughness&quot;. Pretty squishy at face value when compared to a Mummy, Promethean or Werewolf. However, they have a load of ways around that issue and can, given the right combination of effects be the &quot;toughest&quot; template to hit, hurt and keep down. <br /> <br /> I like the feeling of higher stakes and fragility that Demon maintains despite all these powers and traits. It makes the game feel different and stresses the &quot;everything to loose&quot; aspect of he espionage angle the game runs in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T20:25:20-08:00","id":11022,"title":"","content":"You could use wound healing heal the rightmost wound as a reflexive action and then use On the Mend since its instant action if that's what you were asking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T01:33:31-08:00","id":11115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Intrepid Vector</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9746-how-a-demon-dies?p=10099#post10099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>BRING ME THE SOUL OF A FORSAKEN CHILD</b></i><br /> <br /> Edit: Know what could be neat to see? A demon who painstakingly splices together pacts over time to keep recreating more-or-less-the-same Covers as their current one ages too much to be useful. You could play this up as slightly deranged or explain it as sign of how the Demon really identifies with that Cover and is really uncomfortable with the short, transient lifespans of mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a possible way around it though. on the other forums (old WW ones) I had asked if it is possible to have an immortal cover.....someone (dont remember who though atm) said yes, but the it is a compromise if the cover doesn't age.<br /> (also another thing....with patchwork pacts wouldn't it be possible to get the youth from someone and use that on your own cover?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T03:26:35-08:00","id":11145,"title":"","content":"Demons seem tougher than Changelings to me, but I think that's mostly because the Contracts seem a lot more... limited than Embeds and Exploits.<br /> <br /> Catch a Demon by surprise and you can do a lot of damage, but if they survive they have a whole toolbox of tricks they can pull out to get away, depending on how threatened they feel, and if they see you coming they're not too bad even without blowing Cover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T20:45:34-08:00","id":11849,"title":"","content":"Really since your Cover is supposed to act like it's real to the best of it's ability, failing to die would be about the weirdest thing a human could do. You are supposed to be, for the purpose of dealing with reality, a squishy human and thus unless specific countermeasures are put in play you ARE a squishy human, although with the option to drop the bomb on the power scale if needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T04:10:44-08:00","id":12648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pgolasze13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9746-how-a-demon-dies?p=10970#post10970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Mend is pretty powerful. It lets you heal all bashing with a success, one lethal per success or agg equal to your primum. an exceptional success is recover all bashing plus a will power, recover all health lost to lethal or point of agg damage per succes or primum whichever is higher. Thats just an embed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, extremely overpowered fits better. There seems to be no rule avoiding re-using this embed until all damage is gone, and it costs nothing. In my opinion, On the Mend needs to be an exploit, and should cost aether or have some other restrictions.<br /> <br /> Additionally, I was never a fan of powers that can get rid of aggravated damage with an instant action. This is kind of against the concept of &quot;aggravated&quot;, as I understand is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}